AB  - In this paper, we have proposed an improved colour image encryption scheme that combines the Chen chaotic system with a Tribonacci Q-matrix-based block diffusion mechanism. The framework has a three-stage architecture that consists of deterministic permutation, byte-level diffusion, and matrix-based block diffusion that enhances the confusion and diffusion performance. The initial conditions of the Chen chaotic system are derived from the SHA-256 hash of the plaintext image, which ensures strong plaintext sensitivity and deterministic key stream generation. Lexicographic sorting is used to permute the pixel positions, which are controlled by chaotic sequences, while the pixel intensities are modified through modular addition and dynamic bit rotation. We further applied the Tribonacci Q-matrix to non-overlapping 3 × 3 blocks to strengthen the diffusion depth. Security analysis shows near-ideal entropy values, negligible correlation coefficients, uniform histogram distribution and strong resistance against the differential attacks. The large key size 2590 and a 10–14 variation in key parameters result in complete decryption failure, confirming high sensitivity to the secret key.
